From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:15:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ZoneRebalance: the extension's status paragraph in
 public-facing terms, its open endpoint named; a proof sketch for the scratch
 rewind's endpoint; two double blank lines

Docstrings and blank lines only; the code is identical with comments stripped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean    | 23 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
index 77c9119d..e8353f20 100644
--- a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
+++ b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/ZoneRebalance.lean
@@ -634,7 +634,6 @@ private lemma zr_cascade_passes {ℓ : ℕ} (j : ℕ) (z : ZoneContents ℓ) :
   rw [zoneCascadeRight_eq]
   simp only [zr_pair_pass]
 
-
 /-- Positive-level data, indexed by the highest level already present. -/
 private abbrev zr_RightData (k : ℕ) := Σ n : ℕ, Fin k → ZoneContents (n + 1)
 
@@ -978,7 +977,13 @@ private def zr_adjustedBackContract {k : ℕ} (x : List (ZoneSym k)) :=
       simpa only [Set.image_singleton, Option.map_some] using R.exit_mem w d hd hp)
 
 /-- Rewinding scratch after the adjusted walk restores its head and keeps both tapes.
-Only the zoned head remains displaced, by the ruler length. -/
+Only the zoned head remains displaced, by the ruler length.
+
+**Proof sketch.** The contract is the adjusted walk sequenced with skip back and re-wrapped. Its
+precondition gives the walk's; the walk's endpoint (`zr_adjustedWalk_post`) is skip back's
+start (`skipBackTM_contract_post`). Compare the fields: the state and the input position
+directly, both tapes unchanged, the scratch head back at its start and the zoned head advanced
+by `|w|`. -/
 private lemma zr_adjustedBack_post {k : ℕ} {x : List (ZoneSym k)}
     (w : List (ZoneSym k))
     (d : Cfg 2 (ZoneSym k) (((Option Bool) ⊕ SeekPhase) ⊕ SeekPhase) x)
@@ -1142,7 +1147,6 @@ private lemma zr_rightPass_time_le {k : ℕ} {x : List (ZoneSym k)}
   rw [zr_rightPass_time, zoneCapacity_eq, pow_succ]
   omega
 
-
 /-! ### The rows -/
 
 /-- **§13d G4, the rebalance rows** (design §13d, G4; decisions 13d.2–13d.4). For every track
@@ -1223,12 +1227,13 @@ control writes the two cells); write the inner half as all-tracks virtual blanks
 half as all-`⊠` cells; return through home and do the same on the left, through a ruler of the
 distance; clear the ruler and return home. Each phase is `O(2^ℓ)`.
 
-**Implementation status.** A positive-level right-pass contract composes the seeks, ruler
-copy, half-zone writes, adjusted walk, and scratch rewind. Its time is the right-layout extent
-plus ten half-capacities and twenty-three control steps. The corrected left displacement
-includes the separating blank. Return-home rounds, the left pass, the zero-level branch,
-ruler cleanup, and assembly of the complete extension remain open. Only this target's body is
-admitted. -/
+**Implementation status.** A positive-level right-pass contract composes the seek, skip,
+ruler copy, half-zone writes, adjusted walk and scratch rewind, with its exact precondition and
+time (the right-layout extent plus ten half-capacities and twenty-three control steps); its
+endpoint equation and envelope bound are not yet stated. The left displacement, an unadjusted
+walk followed by an adjusted walk across the separating blank, is proved as arithmetic. The
+return-home rounds, the left pass, the zero-level branch, ruler cleanup and the assembly of the
+complete extension remain open. Only this target's body is admitted. -/
 theorem exists_zoneExtendTM (k : ℕ) :
     ∃ (C : ℕ) (S : Type) (_ : Fintype S) (_ : DecidableEq S)
       (M : MultiTapeTM 2 (ZoneSym k) S) (entry done : S),
